<title>GERMANY: Heidelzement sees no reason to reduce '96 dividend.</title>
<headline>Heidelzement sees no reason to reduce '96 dividend.</headline>
<dateline>HEIDELBERG, Germany 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>German building materials group Heidelberger Zement AG said on Wednesday that it saw no reason to reduce its dividend payout for the 1996 business year.</p>
<p>Earlier, the company said it expected its 1996 group net profit to be above the 1995 level of 468.6 million marks and also predicted that sales would rise.</p>
<p>For 1995, Heidelzement paid a dividend of 15 marks per ordinary share and 17 marks per preference share, an increase of one mark from 1994 in each case</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
